      "writtenOn": "2016-09-08T19:57:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question: contrary to chrome in the AP, for the EC, tablet mode means tablet mode: the base is against the lid, screen showing up. Tenting mode is not tablet mode, blocking keyboard in S3 when lid angle \u003e 180 is independant.\n\nThis is already the case for cave, which uses 2 HAL sensors to detect lid position (close (10), open (00), tablet (01))\n(See \n\nWhen we only have one HAL sensor, I use the angle:\n\n\ntablet_mode:\n  1 |                  +-----\u003c----+----------\n    |                  \\/         /\\\n    |                  |          |\n  0 |------------------------\u003e----+\n    +------------------+----------+----------+ lid angle\n    0                 240        300        360\n\n(I like my diagram so much I put it in the code :-))",
